# Normalise line endings.
#
# Everything in this repository is text, and everything that reads it — Python, Node,
# browsers, git — is content with LF. Without this file, edits made on Windows silently
# rewrote whole files as CRLF, and the resulting diffs carried hundreds of lines of noise
# that buried the actual change. One pull request showed 4863 insertions where the real
# figure was closer to 1500.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text; eol=lf pins LF in the repository *and* in the
# working tree, so the drift cannot start again from either direction.
* text=auto eol=lf
